    <briefdescription>
<para>Represents a literal operand in a bitcode record. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The value of a literal operand is the same for all instances of the record, so it is only emitted in the abbreviation definition.</para>
<para>Note that because this uses a compile-time template, you cannot have a literal operand that is fixed at run-time without dropping down to the raw LLVM APIs. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
